 - **Comm fail** is a red button at the strip's edge, always in view and lit while it is on.
-  Beside it is a quick **language switch** (English ⇄ עברית). While your position is live the
+  Beside it is a quick **language switch** (English ⇄ עברית): the other language's name, or a globe when the
+  strip's second line needs the room -- the same in both languages. While your position is live the
   language switch steps aside so the readout keeps its line; **Settings** still has the picker.
 - The readout is measured against its own line, so a part that does not fit is dropped, never
   drawn under the buttons.
